// What a colony calls home. A plain `Solid` -- deliberately the simplest
// thing that renders distinctly and that an ant can stand next to, because
// the nest in v1 is a *sensed material*, not a structure with behaviour.
// `AtNest` is a contact scan for this material and nothing else.
//
// The whole "find your way home" mechanism is elsewhere and is not about
// this file: an ant's channel-A deposit is scaled by how recently it
// touched nest material, so outbound ants paint a gradient that is
// freshest nearest home, and a laden ant walks up it. No ant ever asks
// where the nest is. This material only has to be recognisable on contact.
//
// Pale and warm, to read clearly against soil and against the dark ants
// standing on it.
(
    name: "nest",
    display: "Nest",
    kind: Solid,
    density: 2.0,
    colors: [
        (196, 168, 120),
        (184, 156, 110),
        (206, 180, 132),
    ],
    penetration_resistance: 6.0,
    // **The door is worked soil, so rain soaks into it.** This field was
    // absent -- the default 0, "holds no water at all, and never absorbs an
    // adjacent Liquid" -- and that one omission is the whole of
    // `open-bugs-handoff.md` §T2, the round trip that closed for the founders
    // and then stopped for ever.
    //
    // `paint_nest_patch` converts ~53 surface columns of a misted bed into
    // this material, so the patch was the one impermeable strip on the whole
    // surface of a bed whose every other ground cell holds 1,000. Rain
    // landing on it had nowhere to go and stood as free `water`; an ant
    // cannot step into a liquid (`landing_is_placeable_through_tissue` wants
    // `is_empty`), so the film is a wall, `adjacent_nest` goes false for
    // every animal in the colony, and `AtNest`, `nest_visits` and
    // `deliveries` freeze together. Measured on the played bed, seed 1, over
    // 120,000 frames: of 53 nest cells **47-49 stood under water** and only
    // 2-7 had air beside them, against 3-11 wet of 37 on seed 3 -- the seed
    // whose colony booms. Standing water over the patch against the same
    // width of ordinary ground beside it separated the two readings: the
    // patch floods and the ground either side of it does not.
    //
    // Same 1,000 as `soil` and `packedsoil`, which is what the cell was
    // before the colony worked it and what the colony's own tailings are.
    // `nest` is a `Solid` rather than a `Powder`, which matters in two
    // places and is deliberate in both: the soil-moisture pass filters on
    // this field and not on kind, so the patch drinks and drains normally,
    // while `evaporation`'s soil path is `Powder`-only, so the door gives
    // its water back downward to the column rather than upward to the sky.
    // `weather::water_equivalents` was widened to `Solid | Powder` in the
    // same change so held water here stays on the conservation books.
    //
    // Ablate with `PIXEL_PHYSICS_NEST_DRAINS=off`, which forces this back to
    // 0 -- see `MaterialRegistry::apply_nest_ablation`.
    water_capacity: 1000,
    heat_conductivity: 0.3,
)
